Jira Link: [DB-16505](https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-16505)
### Description

Please see this test case:

```sql
create table t0 (c0 int4);
create table t1 (c1 int4, c2 int4, c3 int4, c4 int4, c5 int4, c6 int4);
create table t2 (c7 int4);
insert into t2 values (14000);
create index i0 on t1 (c4 desc, c3);
create index i1 on t1 (c3 desc, c4 asc, c1, c2 desc, c6 asc, c5);
insert into t1 (c1, c2, c3, c4, c5, c6) values(66, 76000, null, 1, null, -63);
set yb_enable_optimizer_statistics=on;
set yb_enable_base_scans_cost_model=on;
```

```shell
testdb=# select * from t0 right join t1 on(t0.c0 = t1.c3) full join (t2 cross join t1 e) on(t1.c4 = e.c4) where t2.c7 > 0;
 c0 | c1 | c2 | c3 | c4 | c5 | c6 |  c7   | c1 |  c2   | c3 | c4 | c5 | c6  
----+----+----+----+----+----+----+-------+----+-------+----+----+----+-----
    |    |    |    |    |    |    | 14000 | 66 | 76000 |    |  1 |    | -63
```

The result is incorrect, as the first several columns should not be empty. I expect the result is:


```shell
testdb=# select * from t0 right join t1 on(t0.c0 = t1.c3) full join (t2 cross join t1 e) on(t1.c4 = e.c4) where t2.c7 > 0;
 c0 | c1 |  c2   | c3 | c4 | c5 | c6  |  c7   | c1 |  c2   | c3 | c4 | c5 | c6  
----+----+-------+----+----+----+-----+-------+----+-------+----+----+----+-----
    | 66 | 76000 |    |  1 |    | -63 | 14000 | 66 | 76000 |    |  1 |    | -63
```

If we switch off two sets, remove any index, or remove the `where` clause, we can observe the correct result.

